WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.260
Encanto's golden child Isabela was originally
very different, she had a secret boyfriend

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.320
and got married, was a book lover like Belle,
and could grow magical potato people.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.320
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing Isabela's deleted

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.270
scenes and rejected storylines that you never
got to see!

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.710
Some spoilers ahead so take care.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:26.130
One of the funniest moments in the movie is
when the magic goes wrong at Isabela's proposal

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.130
dinner.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.929
As the family's powers misfire, Isa's true
feelings about picture-perfect Mariano sprout

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:35.790
up, subconsciously revealing that she doesn't
want to marry him.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.579
However, in an earlier version of the story,
Isabela had a different boyfriend she chose

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:44.120
herself who she'd meet up with in secret in
the woods.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.289
In an official deleted scene, Mirabel spots
her sister getting dragged into the forest

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:54.579
by a mysterious hooded character, and chases
after her thinking she's in danger.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:01:00.100
Seeing what looks like an animal approach
Isabela, Mirabel attacks the mystery creature

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.510
until she discovers that it's actually...

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:03.530
Bubo Marqués.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.899
Are you alright?

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:10.560
I'm fine, mi amor.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.090
Mi amor?

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.090
Just go home.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.090
You saw nothing.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.189
I wish I saw nothing.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:21.000
What I did see was like two baby birds feeding
each other.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.650
Bubo was from the city so an outsider to the
Encanto, and combined with his quirky personality,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.840
the intention was for him to have a comical,
fish-out-of-water vibe.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.860
I'm wearing this jaguar-print coat.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.340
Wild animals see it and they're like is that
a jaguar?

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.140
And I'm all like, yes!

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.630
And they're like, I will not mess with him.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.360
Most predators hunt by smell.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.290
Which is why I covered it in the urine of
several animals.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.200
The deleted scene continued with Isabela revealing
that she planned to leave the Encanto with

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.710
Bubo, presumably to go to the city.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.200
You're trying to leave?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.390
The place where every person worships the
ground you walk on to go out there?

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.390
Bubo Marqués!

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.790
What is this?

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:00.790
Dark magic?

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:04.450
Bubo is the only person who has ever really
seen me.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.450
And this moment before the barrier is restored
is our only chance to be free.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:14.250
So in this version of Isabela's story, it
appears something had happened to open the

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.780
barrier that kept the Encanto separated from
the outside world.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.730
And perhaps this was an early sign that the
family's magic was weakening.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:26.160
Although there's some humour in this scene
such as Mirabel's reaction to the super-awkward

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.370
kissing, I can see why it was cut as many
of the audience might have found it as uncomfortable

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:37.180
to watch as Mirabel did, and many fans reacted
in horror when they saw this deleted scene.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:42.530
Also, having Bubo as Isabela's love interest
would have shifted the focus of her arc away

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:47.540
from discovering what she wanted for herself
in her life, plus it's kind of cliché in

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.670
terms of its quirky guy and pretty girl trope
we've seen many times before.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.640
In the end, this romantic plot for Isabela
was replaced with Isa rejecting the suitor

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.950
Abuela had lined up for her and making choices
for herself that didn't depend on a love interest.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.480
I never wanted to marry him!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.790
I was doing it for the family!

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.801
An alternate version of the Bubo scene can
also be found in this unused concept art of

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:16.230
a secret garden created by Isabela that Mirabel
wanders into.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.280
It looks like it could have been an amusing
moment and it reminds me a lot of the lilies

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.400
scene in Disney's The Princess and the Frog.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.671
And in another version of Isabela's secret
garden, Mirabel descended into a spiky, dark

00:03:28.671 --> 00:03:32.190
thicket of trees with creepy faces embedded
in the wood.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:37.480
And Bruno, who looked very different in earlier
stories, followed Mirabel into the spooky

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.420
area which was deliberately designed like
that by Isabela to scare people away so they

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.659
wouldn't find out about her secret boyfriend.

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:50.320
Bubo haters will also be shocked to discover
that Isabela was originally going to marry

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.810
him in one of Encanto's epilogues.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:56.909
Clearly from the celebrations, the family
had accepted Bubo by this point;

00:03:56.909 --> 00:04:02.110
and, given the way the bride and groom kiss
here it looks like Isa and Bubo's heavy make-out

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.980
sessions were going to be a running joke in
this version of the story.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:10.850
A fun bonus in this original ending is how
it looks like it was Dolores who caught the

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.860
bridal bouquet and ended up with Mariano,
as she wanted to in the final movie as well.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.860
Yes!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.860
Let's get married..

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.860
Slow down.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:24.470
In an alternate take on the story, Isabela
also loved to read and she created giant hydrangeas

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:29.530
in her room that she and Bubo would lie on,
giving a feeling of them floating on a cloud.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:34.550
In this story, the clouds represented Isabela's
desire to be free and true to herself, while

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.690
at the same time she was "still trapped in
her room".

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.331
This whole shot is stunning, from the detail
of the sun on the floor to the walls made

00:04:42.331 --> 00:04:48.150
of glass which made the room resemble a vase
for putting flowers on display, just as Abuela

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.960
put Isa on display.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:55.009
And you can see Mirabel peeking into the room,
where presumably she would have caught Isa

00:04:55.009 --> 00:04:56.009
with Bubo.

00:04:56.009 --> 00:05:01.699
And I love this little test animation of Isabela
creating a flower seat and plant light bulb

00:05:01.699 --> 00:05:03.070
to read her book.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.660
I wonder if they decided against her being
a book-lover though as that on top of her

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.250
general Disney princess vibe might have made
her feel a little too reminiscent of Belle

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.789
from Beauty and the Beast.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:19.580
There's a small but funny deleted moment from
just before Mirabel hugs it out with her sister,

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.940
where Isabela makes fun of Mirabel by doing
an impression of her with glasses made out

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.190
of her vines.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.870
This would have ended up causing a full-on
fight between the two sisters.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:33.759
I can see why the physical fight was cut though
as it's a little tropey and I think the scene

00:05:33.759 --> 00:05:38.840
we got of Isabela's repressed emotions coming
through as flowers sprouting up in Mirabel's

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:44.400
face was funnier and more interesting as her
anger at having to be constantly perfect finally

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.830
bubbles up to the surface.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:52.020
An amazing concept for Isabela which sadly
didn't make it into the movie was her ability

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.800
to create animated plant creatures, such as
these potato characters.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.110
These living potatoes, dressed in traditional
outfits, would have populated the house and

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.430
even tended their own crops.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.080
Leave a thumbs-up if you love these guys!

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.270
And there was an awesome deleted scene where
they helped Mirabel learn about the history

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:15.080
of a big battle, by re-enacting it together
with an army of magical wallpaper soldiers

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.680
created by Casita.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.550
By the way, Casita's magical wallpaper is
another deleted concept which I'll be discussing

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.770
more in my next video, so make sure you're
subscribed and click the notification bell

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.211
on to get that video.

00:06:29.211 --> 00:06:33.460
In another cut epilogue scene, we can see
that Isabela's door design had both books

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.770
and crossed swords on it and there would have
been a fun moment where she emerged and it

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.130
was revealed that she'd been fencing with
Bubo inside her room where they'd been "role-playing

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.110
something from a book that they had read earlier".

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:49.389
And at one point in the story, Isabela was
going to have a punk-rock look.

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:54.080
I expect this would have come at the moment
when she decided being a Señorita Perfecta

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.699
wasn't what she really wanted so transformed
her look from soft pastel shades to much bolder

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:02.430
colours, ending up with a splatter-paint design.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.419
The punk-rock version of her would have hinted
at an even edgier sense about her newfound

00:07:07.419 --> 00:07:12.349
self, but perhaps it would have been a bit
too cliché for her to go from a classic Disney

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:15.300
princess vibe to a full-on rebel child.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:20.750
And had Bubo made it into the final cut, he
would have also been in the final frame where

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:25.170
one of Bruno's rats takes a picture of the
family and we get the running joke again of

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.740
Isa and Bubo smooching together.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:32.940
In fact, there were even more alternate endings
that were cut from Encanto including a hilarious

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:37.440
post-credits scene with a capybara, plus a
surprise ending for Camilo.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.979
Tap here to learn all about those and there's
also a link in the video description.

00:07:41.979 --> 00:07:46.490
And if you'd like to see more gorgeous concept
art from Encanto, consider getting a copy

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.600
of The Art of Encanto book.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.990
There's a link in the description on how you
can get it with free worldwide shipping.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.610
So, are you a Bubo lover or hater?

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:58.639
And do you wish any of these Isabela deleted
scenes had been in the movie?

00:07:58.639 --> 00:08:00.990
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:05.039
If you enjoyed this video, do leave a thumbs-up,
